    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, I'm Dr. Smith. It's nice to meet you; could you tell me what brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S023",
      "patient_response": "Um, well, my mom is the one who made the appointment. She's just... she's really upset with me because mostly I just can't make myself do anything anymore. Like, nothing at all. I just sit in my room all day. I sit on the edge of my bed, and I've been wearing these exact same clothes—this same oversized hoodie and these pajama pants—for I don't even know how many days now. It's just... it takes too much to take them off, and there's no point anyway. \n\nI don't do any of the stuff I used to do. I used to knit all the time, I was working on this really complicated sweater with cables and everything, and the basket is just sitting right there on the floor, but I don't touch it. I don't touch my journals either, and I used to write pages and pages every single night with these special colored pens I bought. I don't even go out for walks around the neighborhood to get fresh air like I used to. I just sit there staring at the wall. \n\nAnd then my mom comes in, and she stands in the doorway and she keeps asking me, \"What's wrong? Why are you acting like this? What's happening?\" over and over, and she wants this big explanation about my feelings, but I just... I barely have the energy to even look at her, let alone answer. It's like my mouth is too heavy to move and my brain is just empty. So I just stay quiet, and I guess that's why she brought me here, because I just don't have the energy for anything at all.",
