    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "Have you ever experienced a period of time, lasting at least a few days, where you felt unusually energetic, talkative, or euphoric, to the point where you didn't feel like you needed much sleep?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "No, I... I don't think so. I mean, I can't really imagine feeling like that, not right now anyway. Energetic? Euphoric? It's just... it's so far away from how I feel. Like, I told you about how I just sit on the edge of my bed in these same clothes, right? The hoodie and the pajama pants. I just sit there. And sleep... sleep is weird because I don't really feel rested, but I definitely don't feel like I *don't* need it. I just feel heavy all the time. \n\nI don't think I've ever had a time where I was just talking and talking and not sleeping and feeling amazing. Even when I was doing okay, like when I was working on that cabled sweater—the one in the basket on my floor that I haven't touched in forever—or when I was writing in my journals with all those different colored pens every night, I wasn't, like, bouncing off the walls or anything. I was just... doing things. Normal things. And I slept normally, I think. I didn't stay up for days on end feeling like I could take on the world. \n\nMy mom would definitely remember if I had done that, anyway. She notices everything. Like how she keeps standing in my doorway asking me what's wrong and wanting me to explain my feelings when I just... I can't. If I had been running around the house not sleeping and talking a mile a minute, she would have brought it up, or she would have brought me here sooner. But no, it's just been this... this heaviness. This emptiness. So, no, I've never felt like what you're describing. Not for a few days, not for one day. Just... never.",
