    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "Have you ever gone through a period like this in the past, where you felt this same level of heaviness and loss of interest for several weeks or more?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Um, no... I really don't think so. I mean, not like this. I was in high school not that long ago, and sure, I had days where I was tired, like everyone gets tired when they have to study or do homework or whatever. But it wasn't this... this intense gravity. Like, right now, just sitting here, my arms literally feel like they are made out of wet cement. I have never had a time in my life where I couldn't even bring myself to pick up a pen. I told you about those colored pens, right? The special ones I bought for my journals. I used to use them every single night without fail. Even if I had a really bad week or was super stressed out about finishing school, I always wrote pages and pages. \n\nAnd my mom, she wouldn't be acting so confused and upset if this had ever happened before. She keeps standing in my doorway, asking me what is wrong and why I am acting like this, because she has never seen me just sitting on the edge of my bed in this exact same oversized hoodie for days on end. If I had gone through a period like this before, she would probably say something like, oh, you are doing that thing again, let us get you help. But she doesn't say that. She acts like I am a completely alien person that she doesn't even recognize. \n\nSo it has to be the first time. Because I definitely don't remember feeling this incredibly empty, and she clearly doesn't remember it either. I just... I really don't know how everything got so heavy. It just sort of crept up on me and now I am completely stuck in these pajama pants and I can't even look at the knitting basket. It is just sitting there on the floor mocking me. I have never in my life abandoned a sweater before, especially not one with cables. Cables are really hard to do, you have to count all the stitches and keep careful track of the rows, and I was so good at it. I would never just leave it on the floor gathering dust if I didn't have to. So no, I haven't had a time like this. Never anything this heavy.",
